\mt1 List of Abbreviations
\p The list below gives the abbreviations used in the notes. A citation gives the abbreviated book name, chapter, and verse, with an en dash in a range and a semicolon between books; \it Ps.\it* introduces one psalm and \it Pss.\it* several. Of Brenton’s own list we keep the abbreviations the notes still use, reword some of their meanings, and drop the signs and labels the notes no longer print; we add those this edition uses, and arrange them all alphabetically. The signs of the quotation links are explained in the Introduction.
{abbreviations}
